    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d487">

                <pb facs="1073" n="1049" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v24/pg1049"/>

                <head>487. National Security Action Memorandum No. 259<anchor n="0" xml:id="d487-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1963-08-20">August 20,
                        1963</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list type="to">
                    <head>TO</head>
                    <item>The Secretary of State</item>
                    <item>The Director, Agency for International Development</item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Aid Program for Laos—FY 64</item>
                </list>
                <p>The President has approved the proposed FY 64 AID Program for Laos presented in
                    Aidto X–200,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d487-f2"/> subject to the following additional
                    action: <list>
                        <label>(1)</label>
                        <item>Sale of dollars for kip on the open market is to be supervised by an
                            American expert in Vientiane.</item>
                        <label>(2)</label>
                        <item>An agreement with the Lao Government is to be made to hold the budget,
                            and particularly defense expenditures, at current levels.</item>
                        <label>(3)</label>
                        <item>An experienced non-American, non-Lao should be placed in the Laos
                            finance ministry, who is to see that the Lao budget is kept under
                            control and deficit financing is prevented which would neutralize the
                            proposed open-market dollar transactions.</item>
                        <label>(4)</label>
                        <item>The President desires to be informed of actions taken to implement the
                            above.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed>McGeorge Bundy</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
